billion estimates indicate +88% and +65.5% changes, respectively.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e133, e229, e368; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e46 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress on the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said customer forecasts point to NVIDIA's sales growth doubling in FY2028, while NVIDIA expects approximately 70% growth because it is supply-constrained.\n    Quote: Customer forecasts point to our growth doubling next year. However, as I mentioned earlier, we expect to grow approximately 70% as we are supply-constrained.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44, e63, e77, e132; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e47 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang on the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call; original source NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI agents use between 15 and 100 times as much compute as work guided by a human, increasing computing needs.\n    Quote: the amount of compute necessary is just extraordinary\n- e48 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source S&P Global ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] S&P Global forecast that tech companies will spend an estimated $1.3 trillion on AI in calendar 2027.\n    Quote: S&P Global recently forecast that tech companies will spend an estimated $1.3 trillion on AI next year.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e222; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-23; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] The author reported that demand for Micron memory chips far outpaces supply, driving sharply higher memory prices and supply constraints.\n    Quote: Micron Technology 's memory chips are having a significant problem, with demand far outpacing supply. That's led to skyrocketing memory prices, higher margins for Micron, and global supply constraints.\n- e50 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang on the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call; original source NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said most AI had recently shifted to being agentic and predicted that every company would have many AI agents.\n    Quote: Today, the vast majority of AI is prompted by people. I believe that this last month, it has crossed. Most AI are now agentic. But in the future, every company will have a whole bunch of agents.\n- e51 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA said it is working to increase supply to meet customer demand.\n    Quote: Nvidia says it's working to increase supply to meet customer demand.\n- e57 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St. author; original source 24/7 Wall St. author 2026-09-23; from gnews:dac89e12f005c43e4ec94571 2026-09-23] The 24/7 Wall St. author forecast hyperscaler capital spending of nearly $800 billion in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\n    Quote: Hyperscaler capex is expected to reach nearly 800 billion in 2026 and 1.3 trillion in 2027, a wave that also pulls in the power, cooling, and networking suppliers we profiled in a free report on seven AI infrastructure names that aren't chipmakers.\n- e65 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Daniel Sparks 2026-09-23; from gnews:ef6c9a018d21f7762df0efde 2026-09-23] The author calculated that Nvidia shares at $227.38 traded at about 15 times expected FY2028 earnings.\n    Quote: At Monday's close of $227.38, shares trade at about 15 times what the company is