{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"awk '/\"'^## Question/{q=$0} /''^- e[0-9]+ '\"\\\\[/{print q, \"'$0} /''^'\"\\\\*\\\\*How much/{print} /\"'^- [1-5] /{print} /''^### The stored answer/{s=1} s && !/''^```/{print} /''^## Question Q/{s=0}'\"' /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/duplicates/pair-fy2028.md\"","aggregated_output":"**How much total revenue will Nvidia report for FY2028?**\n- 1 Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least 739145000000 USD.\n- 2 Bullish: Total revenue is at least 692108500000 USD and below 739145000000 USD.\n- 3 Neutral: Total revenue is at least 651791500000 USD and below 692108500000 USD.\n- 4 Bearish: Total revenue is at least 604755000000 USD and below 651791500000 USD.\n- 5 Strongly bearish: Total revenue is below 604755000000 USD.\n## Question P - e5 [third_party_view; Zacks.com analyst; original source Zacks 2026-09-22; from gnews:1cad3125b4e74ed0c1ae1389 2026-09-22] Zacks estimated Nvidia total revenue at $406.05 billion for FY2027, up 88% year over year.\n## Question P - e46 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress on the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said customer forecasts point to NVIDIA's sales growth doubling in FY2028, while NVIDIA expects approximately 70% growth because it is supply-constrained.\n## Question P - e47 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang on the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call; original source NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI agents use between 15 and 100 times as much compute as work guided by a human, increasing computing needs.\n## Question P - e48 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source S&P Global ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] S&P Global forecast that tech companies will spend an estimated $1.3 trillion on AI in calendar 2027.\n## Question P - e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-23; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] The author reported that demand for Micron memory chips far outpaces supply, driving sharply higher memory prices and supply constraints.\n## Question P - e50 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang on the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call; original source NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said most AI had recently shifted to being agentic and predicted that every company would have many AI agents.\n## Question P - e51 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA said it is working to increase supply to meet customer demand.\n## Question P - e57 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St. author; original source 24/7 Wall St. author 2026-09-23; from gnews:dac89e12f005c43e4ec94571 2026-09-23] The 24/7 Wall St. author forecast hyperscaler capital spending of nearly $800 billion in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\n## Question P - e65 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Daniel Sparks 2026-09-23; from gnews:ef6c9a018d21f7762df0efde 2026-09-23] The author calculated that Nvidia shares at $227.38 traded at about 15 times expected FY2028 earnings.\n## Question P - e90 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Keithen Drury 2026-09-23; from gnews:915fe84b4c7f7b4decd1665d 2026-09-23] The author said Broadcom and its AI hyperscaler clients are designing workload-specific AI computing units that perform AI computing at lower cost and more effectively than Nvidia's GPUs, threatening Nvidia's market share.\n## Question P - e94 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:915fe84b4c7f7b4decd1665d 2026-09-23] Nvidia projected that global annual data-center capital expenditures would reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\n## Question P - e99 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), reporting Huang's remarks to reporters; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:e48962399352b7dd987d4ffe 2026-09-24] Jensen Huang suggested Nvidia's chip sales would double in the coming year.\n## Question P - e125 [party_statement; FreightWaves; original source Einride 2026-09-21; from gnews:218a1690c55690272864d245 2026-09-24] Einride expects its vehicle footprint to reach 1,500 to 2,000 vehicles by 2028, based on customer demand captured on its platform.\n## Question P - e126 [party_statement; FreightWaves; original source Einride 2026-09-21; from gnews:218a1690c55690272864d245 2026-09-24] Einride said about 80% of the customer demand captured on its platform is suitable for automation in the medium term.\n## Question P - e127 [third_party_view; The author, quoting Ramez Naam from the August 4 Moonshots episode.; original source Ramez Naam 2026-08-04; from gnews:96dcea7852c4dd5b6c3f747e 2026-09-24] Ramez Naam said on August 4, 2026, that NVIDIA’s CUDA moat is broken in 2026 and 2027.\n## Question P - e128 [third_party_view; The author, reporting Dave Blundin’s conclusion from the August Moonshots discussion.; original source Dave Blundin ; from gnews:96dcea7852c4dd5b6c3f747e 2026-09-24] Dave Blundin judged that CUDA no longer provides an inference-time moat and has only a limited remaining lifespan as a training-time moat.\n## Question P - e129 [third_party_view; The author, reporting Dave Blundin’s view from the August Moonshots discussion.; original source Dave Blundin ; from gnews:96dcea7852c4dd5b6c3f747e 2026-09-24] Dave Blundin estimated that 90–95% of AI workload is moving to inference.\n## Question P - e130 [third_party_view; The author, reporting Dave Blundin’s account.; original source Dave Blundin ; from gnews:96dcea7852c4dd5b6c3f747e 2026-09-24] Dave Blundin said he had written custom kernels for Fable 5 himself over the preceding few weeks, work he said previously required a team of specialists and could now be done with a prompt.\n## Question P - e132 [party_statement; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7fb0b2b7d22b8bb07625b212 2026-09-24] NVIDIA expects FY2028 revenue growth of about 70%; the article says supply constraints could limit the pace of meeting demand.\n## Question P - e135 [third_party_view; Zacks.com; original source AMD ; from gnews:7fb0b2b7d22b8bb07625b212 2026-09-24] AMD's Helios platform is in production, with initial shipments expected late in 2026 Q3 and a larger ramp-up expected in Q4 2026 and 2027.\n## Question P - e136 [fact; Zacks.com; original source Anthropic ; from gnews:7fb0b2b7d22b8bb07625b212 2026-09-24] Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 GW of AMD MI450-series GPUs on Helios, with the first 1 GW planned to begin in the first half of 2027.\n## Question P - e137 [fact; Zacks.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7fb0b2b7d22b8bb07625b212 2026-09-24] Microsoft plans to deploy AMD's Helios platform at scale on Azure.\n## Question P - e138 [party_statement; Zacks.com; original source AMD ; from gnews:7fb0b2b7d22b8bb07625b212 2026-09-24] AMD expects its Data Center segment revenue to more than double year over year in 2027.\n## Question P - e157 [third_party_view; Trefis, the article’s author; original source Trefis, the article’s author 2026-09-24; from gnews:06218d9421731e5e59c1dbef 2026-09-24] Trefis reported that consensus estimates had NVIDIA earnings and revenue growing at a similar pace from FY2027 to FY2028, implying roughly steady profit margins.\n## Question P - e159 [party_statement; semafor.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:73ad0caddfdd9ae934f00920 2026-09-24] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said Nvidia’s chip sales would double next year; the item does not specify the sales measure or year.\n## Question P - e161 [fact; Cloud Wars, reporting the announcement; original source AWS and NVIDIA 2026-09-24; from gnews:7c4283c55cf02ba9cfd9a835 2026-09-24] AWS and NVIDIA announced a plan to deploy 2 million additional NVIDIA GPUs across AWS infrastructure between 2027 and 2028.\n## Question P - e162 [fact; Cloud Wars, reporting the announcement; original source Amazon Robotics and NVIDIA 2026-09-24; from gnews:7c4283c55cf02ba9cfd9a835 2026-09-24] Amazon Robotics plans to integrate NVIDIA’s full-stack physical AI platform into its robotics projects.\n## Question P - e163 [fact; Cloud Wars, reporting the announcement; original source AWS and NVIDIA 2026-09-24; from gnews:7c4283c55cf02ba9cfd9a835 2026-09-24] AWS and NVIDIA plan to build AI factories for the U.S. government, enabling delivery of 100,000 GPUs on AWS secure infrastructure for federal and national-security workloads.\n## Question P - e181 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:a6d9db55f2f71f072c5ba33c 2026-09-25] NVIDIA management expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028.\n## Question P - e186 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:a6d9db55f2f71f072c5ba33c 2026-09-25] NVIDIA management expects AI labs backed by NVIDIA’s balance sheet to account for roughly one-quarter of NVIDIA’s business in fiscal 2028.\n## Question P - e187 [third_party_view; trefis.com; original source trefis.com 2026-09-25; from gnews:a6d9db55f2f71f072c5ba33c 2026-09-25] The author calculated NVIDIA revenue growth of 83% over the past year, compared with 16.7% for Texas Instruments.\n## Question P - e189 [party_statement; MarketBeat; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:91b917994e36036e304616e8 2026-09-25] MarketBeat reports that NVIDIA forecasts doubling its chip volume next year (2027).\n## Question P - e196 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4c4c114117f5c7acb7be91f7 2026-09-25] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said the company expects fiscal 2028 revenue to grow roughly 70%.\n## Question P - e197 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4c4c114117f5c7acb7be91f7 2026-09-25] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress characterized the fiscal 2028 revenue outlook as supply-constrained, with manufacturing capacity limiting revenue rather than customer demand.\n## Question P - e199 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-25; from gnews:4c4c114117f5c7acb7be91f7 2026-09-25] The author calculated that applying roughly 70% growth to the $412 billion fiscal 2027 consensus estimate implies around $700 billion of NVIDIA fiscal 2028 revenue.\n## Question P - e201 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-25; from gnews:4c4c114117f5c7acb7be91f7 2026-09-25] The author expects NVIDIA's earnings to come in more or less as forecast.\n## Question P - e246 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:030fdadd39d106b9a582bbe5 2026-09-26] Broadcom expects AI semiconductor revenue of $115 billion in FY2027 and $230 billion in FY2028.\n## Question P - e255 [party_statement; currently.att.yahoo.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:24ce0978052875d95cce2ab2 2026-09-26] Broadcom expected AI semiconductor revenue of $230 billion in FY2028.\n## Question P - e271 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury, fool.com; original source Keithen Drury 2026-09-26; from gnews:7a1c5168f62af67f4e1fbe93 2026-09-26] Keithen Drury estimates Broadcom AI semiconductor revenue will exceed $115 billion in 2027, more than doubling and growing faster than NVIDIA.\n## Question P - e272 [party_statement; Keithen Drury, fool.com; original source Micron ; from gnews:7a1c5168f62af67f4e1fbe93 2026-09-26] Micron does not expect tightness in the memory-chip market to ease before 2028.\n## Question P - e277 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-09-27; from gnews:3cb10ae6c791ea2937ab87e2 2026-09-27] The author forecasts that Nvidia will generate more quarterly revenue than Apple by 2027.\n## Question P - e286 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author, reporting Musk's comments; original source Elon Musk ; from gnews:33aa3209db96726fbc8fdc92 2026-09-27] Elon Musk said earlier in September 2026 that SpaceX planned to use Nvidia chips exclusively going forward.\n## Question P - e287 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author, reporting Musk's comments; original source Elon Musk ; from gnews:33aa3209db96726fbc8fdc92 2026-09-27] Musk said SpaceX expected to reach around 2 GW of computing power by the end of 2026 and was targeting closer to 10 GW than 5 GW by the end of 2027.\n## Question P - e288 [third_party_view; The Motley Fool author; original source The Motley Fool author 2026-09-27; from gnews:33aa3209db96726fbc8fdc92 2026-09-27] The author estimated that 1 GW of computing power costs about $50 billion to $60 billion, including about $35 billion of Nvidia chips and other components.\n## Question P - e319 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:d4f3bddf04a4d029a097541c 2026-09-27] NVIDIA management expected supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028.\n## Question P - e325 [third_party_view; How-To Geek author Monica J. White; original source How-To Geek author Monica J. White 2026-09-27; from gnews:382aee425dc6b77586e1c456 2026-09-27] How-To Geek reported that the retail prices of NVIDIA’s RTX 5060 Ti 16GB and RTX 5070 Ti had risen to around $800 and $1,200, respectively, from launch MSRPs of $429 and $749; the article gives no specific date for the price observations.\n## Question P - e345 [party_statement; cnbc.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:02b796f20d201c8380e0ae4d 2026-09-28] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the company would double the number of chips it sells in calendar 2027.\n### The stored answer of question P (2026-09-28)\n\n- Answer: 2\n- Reference: NVIDIA's FY2028 revenue market estimate is $671.95 billion (e5), placing the reference in rung 3: at least $651.7915 billion and below $692.1085 billion.\n- What it expects: About $700 billion: apply management's roughly 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the $412 billion FY2027 consensus base ($412 billion × 1.70), as calculated in e199. This is above rung 2's $692.1085 billion floor but below rung 1's $739.145 billion floor.\n- Reasons: The market reference is NVIDIA's FY2028 revenue estimate of $671.95 billion, which is rung 3. The stronger forecast input is management's roughly 70% FY2028 growth outlook: applying it to the $412 billion FY2027 consensus base gives about $700 billion, in rung 2. That estimate is close to rung 2's $692.1085 billion floor: using Zacks' lower $406.05 billion FY2027 estimate instead would imply about $690 billion, just below the boundary. The additional customer-demand announcements support the outlook but do not give a reliable FY2028 revenue conversion; the SpaceX target is a capacity ambition, not confirmed NVIDIA revenue, and management expects supply constraints through FY2028. The central forecast therefore remains rung 2, with limited margin over rung 3.\n\n## Question Q\n**How much will Nvidia's total revenue grow in FY2028?**\n- 1 Strongly bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 80%.\n- 2 Bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 70% and below 80%.\n- 3 Neutral: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 45% and below 70%.\n- 4 Bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 25% and below 45%.\n- 5 Strongly bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is below 25%.\n## Question Q - e13 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source Colette Kress ; from gnews:355e074116b277efe4dcaaab 2026-09-22] Nvidia CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in FY2028, versus 45% previously modeled by Wall Street, according to the author.\n## Question Q - e44 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:aa0d7cffe1e3c710b6347ad4 2026-09-23] Nvidia guided to about 70% revenue growth for FY2028.\n## Question Q - e46 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress on the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said customer forecasts point to NVIDIA's sales growth doubling in FY2028, while NVIDIA expects approximately 70% growth because it is supply-constrained.\n## Question Q - e59 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:b27439abc0c0e249a9a8bbc9 2026-09-23] The author says Wall Street expects Nvidia revenue growth of 91% in FY2027 and 66% in FY2028.\n## Question Q - e62 [party_statement; Colette Kress, quoted by fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Colette Kress, Nvidia CFO ; from gnews:ef6c9a018d21f7762df0efde 2026-09-23] Nvidia CFO Colette Kress expected Nvidia revenue to grow approximately 70% in FY2028.\n## Question Q - e63 [party_statement; Colette Kress, quoted by fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Colette Kress, Nvidia CFO ; from gnews:ef6c9a018d21f7762df0efde 2026-09-23] Nvidia CFO Colette Kress characterized the company's FY2028 revenue outlook as supply-constrained.\n## Question Q - e64 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Jensen Huang, Nvidia CEO ; from gnews:ef6c9a018d21f7762df0efde 2026-09-23] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said customer demand without the supply constraint would be a lot higher.\n## Question Q - e90 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Keithen Drury 2026-09-23; from gnews:915fe84b4c7f7b4decd1665d 2026-09-23] The author said Broadcom and its AI hyperscaler clients are designing workload-specific AI computing units that perform AI computing at lower cost and more effectively than Nvidia's GPUs, threatening Nvidia's market share.\n## Question Q - e94 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:915fe84b4c7f7b4decd1665d 2026-09-23] Nvidia projected that global annual data-center capital expenditures would reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\n## Question Q - e132 [party_statement; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7fb0b2b7d22b8bb07625b212 2026-09-24] NVIDIA expects FY2028 revenue growth of about 70%; the article says supply constraints could limit the pace of meeting demand.\n## Question Q - e152 [party_statement; Trefis, relaying NVIDIA management’s guidance; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:06218d9421731e5e59c1dbef 2026-09-24] NVIDIA management guided to about 70% total revenue growth in FY2028, its first full-year-ahead revenue growth guidance.\n## Question Q - e153 [party_statement; Trefis, relaying NVIDIA’s CEO; original source NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:06218d9421731e5e59c1dbef 2026-09-24] NVIDIA’s CEO said demand supports revenue growth well above 70% for FY2028, but supply limits the guidance to about 70%.\n## Question Q - e154 [party_statement; Trefis, relaying NVIDIA’s CFO; original source NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:06218d9421731e5e59c1dbef 2026-09-24] NVIDIA’s CFO expected supply to remain a bottleneck through at least the end of FY2028 and described memory pricing as extreme.\n## Question Q - e157 [third_party_view; Trefis, the article’s author; original source Trefis, the article’s author 2026-09-24; from gnews:06218d9421731e5e59c1dbef 2026-09-24] Trefis reported that consensus estimates had NVIDIA earnings and revenue growing at a similar pace from FY2027 to FY2028, implying roughly steady profit margins.\n## Question Q - e159 [party_statement; semafor.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:73ad0caddfdd9ae934f00920 2026-09-24] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said Nvidia’s chip sales would double next year; the item does not specify the sales measure or year.\n## Question Q - e161 [fact; Cloud Wars, reporting the announcement; original source AWS and NVIDIA 2026-09-24; from gnews:7c4283c55cf02ba9cfd9a835 2026-09-24] AWS and NVIDIA announced a plan to deploy 2 million additional NVIDIA GPUs across AWS infrastructure between 2027 and 2028.\n## Question Q - e162 [fact; Cloud Wars, reporting the announcement; original source Amazon Robotics and NVIDIA 2026-09-24; from gnews:7c4283c55cf02ba9cfd9a835 2026-09-24] Amazon Robotics plans to integrate NVIDIA’s full-stack physical AI platform into its robotics projects.\n## Question Q - e163 [fact; Cloud Wars, reporting the announcement; original source AWS and NVIDIA 2026-09-24; from gnews:7c4283c55cf02ba9cfd9a835 2026-09-24] AWS and NVIDIA plan to build AI factories for the U.S. government, enabling delivery of 100,000 GPUs on AWS secure infrastructure for federal and national-security workloads.\n## Question Q - e181 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:a6d9db55f2f71f072c5ba33c 2026-09-25] NVIDIA management expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028.\n## Question Q - e186 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:a6d9db55f2f71f072c5ba33c 2026-09-25] NVIDIA management expects AI labs backed by NVIDIA’s balance sheet to account for roughly one-quarter of NVIDIA’s business in fiscal 2028.\n## Question Q - e187 [third_party_view; trefis.com; original source trefis.com 2026-09-25; from gnews:a6d9db55f2f71f072c5ba33c 2026-09-25] The author calculated NVIDIA revenue growth of 83% over the past year, compared with 16.7% for Texas Instruments.\n## Question Q - e196 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4c4c114117f5c7acb7be91f7 2026-09-25] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said the company expects fiscal 2028 revenue to grow roughly 70%.\n## Question Q - e197 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4c4c114117f5c7acb7be91f7 2026-09-25] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress characterized the fiscal 2028 revenue outlook as supply-constrained, with manufacturing capacity limiting revenue rather than customer demand.\n## Question Q - e199 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-25; from gnews:4c4c114117f5c7acb7be91f7 2026-09-25] The author calculated that applying roughly 70% growth to the $412 billion fiscal 2027 consensus estimate implies around $700 billion of NVIDIA fiscal 2028 revenue.\n## Question Q - e201 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-25; from gnews:4c4c114117f5c7acb7be91f7 2026-09-25] The author expects NVIDIA's earnings to come in more or less as forecast.\n## Question Q - e236 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-26; from gnews:f72f4de1d44f4ee9244c7f89 2026-09-26] The author expected Nvidia total revenue to grow 70% next year.\n## Question Q - e255 [party_statement; currently.att.yahoo.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:24ce0978052875d95cce2ab2 2026-09-26] Broadcom expected AI semiconductor revenue of $230 billion in FY2028.\n## Question Q - e268 [party_statement; Keithen Drury, fool.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:7a1c5168f62af67f4e1fbe93 2026-09-26] NVIDIA management believes NVIDIA revenue will grow 70% in 2027.\n## Question Q - e269 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury, fool.com; original source Keithen Drury 2026-09-26; from gnews:7a1c5168f62af67f4e1fbe93 2026-09-26] Keithen Drury estimates NVIDIA’s 2027 revenue growth will exceed management’s 70% expectation.\n## Question Q - e276 [party_statement; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3cb10ae6c791ea2937ab87e2 2026-09-27] Nvidia projects 70% revenue growth for next year, with continued GPU supply-demand imbalance contributing to the forecast.\n## Question Q - e293 [party_statement; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3e0b54b2bb227716c646f29f 2026-09-27] Nvidia projected that 