o 66% (e59) FY2028 revenue growth, placing the reference in rung 3.\n- What it expects: About 70% FY2028 growth: management's direct outlook is approximately 70%, and applying that growth to the cited $412 billion FY2027 consensus base implies roughly $700 billion of FY2028 revenue (e199). The supply constraint expected through FY2028 limits the case for exceeding that outlook.\n- Reasons: The market reference is roughly 65.5%–66% FY2028 growth, which is rung 3 (45% to below 70%). NVIDIA's approximately 70% FY2028 guidance is the stronger forecast input and sits exactly at rung 2's lower boundary. The supply bottleneck expected to last through FY2028 constrains the upside implied by customer demand; the AWS and federal GPU deployments support demand but span multiple years and do not provide enough FY2028 revenue or pricing detail to raise the implied outcome above the guide. Thus the implied outcome remains about 70%, rung 2.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
