the article gives no specific date for the price observations.\n    Quote: Just to give you a couple of examples, the RTX 5060 Ti 16GB launched with a $429 MSRP, and it now costs around $800 , while the RTX 5070 Ti launched at $749 but now costs around $1,200 .\n- e345 [party_statement; cnbc.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:02b796f20d201c8380e0ae4d 2026-09-28] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the company would double the number of chips it sells in calendar 2027.\n    Quote: Huang earlier this month said Nvidia would double the number of chips it sells in 2027.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e189; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n\n[Themes in force, 5]\n- v14 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology permit Alibaba and ByteDance to buy Nvidia RTX PRO 5500 cards by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-28; reasons: The reference is rung 2 (no permission by the deadline): no market consensus or confirmed permission is supplied, so the reference is the no-permission status. The forecast is rung 1 because the report that MIIT intends to approve purchases, together with its request for Alibaba's and ByteDance's pl\n- v15 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology approve domestic firms' purchases of Nvidia RTX Pro 5500 GPUs by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-27; reasons: The reference is rung 2 because no market consensus or formal approval timetable is supplied, so the no-approval-by-deadline outcome is the baseline rather than a reported expectation. The evidence shifts the forecast to rung 1: the reported request for purchase plans and stated intent to approve ma\n- v6 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will the U.S. administration authorize Nvidia Blackwell chip exports to China by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 No; judged 2026-09-28; reasons: The available reference is the existing U.S. restriction on Nvidia's most advanced chips, which places the expectation at rung 1; no Blackwell-specific consensus or guidance is supplied. The evidence implies that authorization of Blackwell by January 31, 2027 remains less likely than non-authorizati\n- v7 (ai-capex, due 2027-04-30) How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend on data centers in calendar 2026?: now rung 3 $775 billion to below $825 billion; judged 2026-09-26; reasons: The reference is nearly $800 billion for calendar 2026, which sits in rung 3 ($775 billion to below $825 billion). The evidence still implies a total near $800 billion, so it does not cross either boundary. The energy comments and financing concerns identify possible constraints or risks but give no\n- v8 (ai-capex, due 2028-12-31) How much will tech companies spend on AI in calendar 2027?: now rung 3 Middle range; judged 2026-09-28; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference is about $1.3 trillion for 2027, which sits in rung 3 ($1.2 trillion to below $1.4 trillion). The direct estimate for tech-company AI spending remains about $1.3 trillion; the hyperscaler capex figures support the scale but are not added to that broader estimate. S&P Global Ratings' pr\n\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 2; reasons: The market reference is Zacks' FY2028 estimate of $671.95 billion, which sits in rung 3. The stronger forecast input is NVIDIA's roughly 70% FY2028 growth outlook: applying it to the $412 billion FY2027 consensus base implies about $700 billion, in rung 2. The announced AWS GPU deployments add evidence of demand, but do not state revenue or provide a price-to-revenue conversion; the company also expects supply constraints through FY2028. The implied figure therefore remains above rung 2's $692.1085 billion floor but below rung 1's $739.145 billion floor.\n\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\n```\n\n### The stored answer of question P (2026-09-28)\n\n- Answer: 2\n- Reference: NVIDIA's FY2028 revenue market estimate is $671.95 billion (e5), placing the reference in rung 3: at least $651.7915 billion and below $692.1085 billion.\n- What it expects: About $700 billion: apply management's roughly 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the $412 billion FY2027 consensus base ($412 billion × 1.70), as calculated in e199. This is above rung 2's $692.1085 billion floor but below rung 1's $739.145 billion floor.\n- Reasons: The market reference is NVIDIA's FY2028 revenue estimate of $671.95 billion, which is rung 3. The stronger forecast input is management's roughly 70% FY2028 growth outlook: applying it to the $412 billion FY2027 consensus base gives about $700 billion, in rung 2. That estimate is close to rung 2's $692.1085 billion floor: using Zacks' lower $406.05 billion FY2027 estimate instead would imply about $690 billion, just below the boundary. The additional customer-demand announcements support the outlook but do not give a reliable FY2028 revenue conversion; the SpaceX target is a capacity ambition, not confirmed NVIDIA revenue, and management expects supply constraints through FY2028. The central forecast therefore remains rung 2, with limited margin over rung 3.\n\n## Question Q\n\n**How much will Nvidia's total revenue grow in FY2028?**\n\nOpened at article 22 of the week; due 2028-02-29; 43 statements linked, 39 of them printed in this request. Possible answers:\n\n- 1 Strongly bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 80%.\n- 2 Bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 70% and below 80%.\n- 3 Neutral: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 45% and below 70%.\n- 4 Bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 25% and below 45%.\n- 5 Strongly bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is below 25%.\n\n### The request of question Q's latest judgement (2026-09-28), as the judge received it\n\n```\nThesis v5 (NVDA, asset, focus \"FY2028 total revenue growth\", FY2028, due 2028-02-29): How much will Nvidia's total revenue grow in FY2028?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 80%. / rung 2 Bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 70% and below 80%. / rung 3 Neutral: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 45% and below 70%. / rung 4 Bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 25% and below 45%. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is below 25%.\n\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 39 items]\n[Not shown: 4 more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]\n- e13 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source Colette Kress ; from gnews:355e074116b277efe4dcaaab 2026-09-22] Nvidia CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in FY2028, versus 45% previously modeled by Wall Street, according to the author.\n    Quote: CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — a figure that far exceeded the 45% Wall Street had previously modeled.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e44 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:aa0d7cffe1e3c710b6347ad4 2026-09-23] Nvidia guided to about 70% revenue growth for FY2028.\n    Quote: issued bullish guidance for about 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e13, e46, e56, e62, e70, e152, e360, e371; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e46 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress on the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:46b3435210a9cc3557b44d78 2026-09-23] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said customer forecasts point to NVIDIA's sales growth doubling in FY2028, while NVIDIA expects approximately 70% growth because it is supply-constrained.\n    Quote: Customer forecasts point to our growth doubling next year. However, as I mentioned earlier, we expect to grow approximately 70% as we are supply-constrained.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44, e63, e77, e132; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e59 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:b27439abc0c0e249a9a8bbc9 2026-09-23] The author says Wall Street expects Nvidia revenue growth of 91% in FY2027 and 66% in FY2028.\n    Quote: Wall Street expects the company to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year.\n- e62 [party_statement; Colette Kress, quoted by fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Colette Kress, Nvidia CFO ; from gnews:ef6c9a018d21f7762df0efde 2026-09-23] Nvidia CFO Colette Kress expected Nvidia revenue to grow approximately 70% in FY2028.\n    Quote: We expect to grow revenue by approximately 70% in fiscal 2028,\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"A September 22 Barchart article said Wall Street had previously modeled 45% FY2028 revenue growth before Nvidia's 70% guidance.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e13\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e46\",\"e132\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The earlier estimate gives context for how much expectations changed before the FY2028 revenue forecast.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"A September 23 article reported that Wall Street expected Nvidia revenue growth of 91% in FY2027 and 66% in FY2028.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e59\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e5\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Those growth estimates provide another market reference for projecting FY2028 revenue.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"Trefis reported on September 24 that Nvidia's approximately 70% FY2028 revenue-growth guidance was its first full-year-ahead revenue-growth guidance.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e152\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e132\",\"e196\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The novelty of the guidance is context an analyst could weigh when judging its reliability.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said demand supported FY2028 revenue growth well above 70%, but supply limited the outlook to about 70%.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e64\",\"e153\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e46\",\"e197\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The CEO's assessment describes potential demand above the supply-limited revenue outlook.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"Nvidia's CFO described memory pricing as extreme in a report published September 24.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e154\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e49\",\"e181\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Extreme memory pricing could affect the cost and availability of components used in Nvidia systems.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"Keithen Drury estimated on September 26 that Nvidia's 2027 revenue growth would exceed management's 70% expectation.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e269\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e46\",\"e132\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"A forecast above management's growth outlook could imply higher FY2028 revenue.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"Nvidia reported that its share of IT capital spending among the five largest cloud providers rose from 11% in the first quarter of 2023 and projected it would reach 44% by 2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e351\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"A growing share of major customers' spending could support Nvidia's revenue outlook.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Zacks estimated on September 22 that Nvidia's FY2027 revenue would be $406.05 billion and its FY2028 revenue would be $671.95 billion.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e5\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e368\",\"e199\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The revenue estimates provide a base and an implied growth forecast to compare with the possible growth ranges.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Jensen Huang said AI agents use 15 to 100 times as much compute as work guided by a human.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e47\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e371\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Higher computing requirements could increase demand for Nvidia products and affect revenue growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"S&P Global forecast that tech companies would spend an estimated $1.3 trillion on AI in calendar 2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e48\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The forecast describes the scale of spending that could support Nvidia's revenue growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"A Motley Fool author reported on September 23 that demand for Micron memory chips far exceeded supply, driving sharply higher prices and supply constraints.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e49\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e154\",\"e181\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Memory shortages could constrain the supply of Nvidia systems and therefore revenue growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Jensen Huang said most AI had recently shifted to being agentic and predicted that every company would have many AI agents.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e50\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e371\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The adoption of AI agents could affect demand for the computing products behind Nvidia's growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Nvidia said it was working to increase supply to meet customer demand, according to a September 23 article.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e51\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e197\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Increasing supply could allow Nvidia to convert more demand into revenue.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"A 24/7 Wall St. author forecast nearly $800 billion in hyperscaler capital spending in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e57\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Hyperscaler spending is relevant to potential demand for Nvidia's data-center products.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Daniel Sparks calculated on September 23 that Nvidia shares at $227.38 traded at about 15 times expected FY2028 earnings.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e65\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The share valuation does not itself forecast FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Einride said on September 21 that it expected its vehicle footprint to reach 1,500 to 2,000 vehicles by 2028 based on captured customer demand.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e125\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The statement does not identify Nvidia revenue or a connection to Nvidia's FY2028 growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Einride said on September 21 that about 80% of the customer demand captured on its platform was suitable for automation in the medium term.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e126\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The statement does not identify demand for Nvidia products or its effect on FY2028 revenue.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Ramez Naam said on August 4, 2026, that Nvidia's CUDA moat was broken in 2026 and 2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e127\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e90\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"A weaker software advantage could make it easier for competitors to win demand from Nvidia.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Dave Blundin concluded that CUDA no longer provided an inference-time moat and had only a limited remaining lifespan as a training-time moat.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e128\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e90\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"His assessment could affect expectations for Nvidia's competitive position and revenue growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Dave Blundin estimated that 90–95% of AI workload was moving to inference.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e129\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e371\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"A shift toward inference could change the demand Nvidia faces and the competitive alternatives available to customers.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Dave Blundin said he had recently written custom kernels for Fable 5 himself using prompts, work he said previously required a team of specialists.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e130\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e90\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Easier development of custom software could affect how strongly Nvidia's software ecosystem protects its sales.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"AMD said its Helios platform was in production, with initial shipments expected late in the third quarter of 2026 and a larger ramp in the fourth quarter and 2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e135\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e90\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The availability of a competing platform could affect Nvidia's share of AI infrastructure spending.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Anthropic planned to deploy up to 2 GW of AMD MI450-series GPUs on Helios, with the first 1 GW beginning in the first half of 2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e136\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e90\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"A major customer's planned use of competing GPUs could affect Nvidia's growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Microsoft planned to deploy AMD's Helios platform at scale on Azure.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e137\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e90\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"A large cloud provider's adoption of a competing platform could affect Nvidia's sales.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"AMD expected its data-center revenue to more than double year over year in 2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e138\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e90\",\"e255\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Rapid growth at a competitor could affect expectations for Nvidia's market share.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Broadcom expected $115 billion in AI semiconductor revenue in FY2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e246\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e255\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"A competing supplier's expected revenue provides context for the pace of competition facing Nvidia.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Keithen Drury estimated on September 26 that Broadcom's AI semiconductor revenue would exceed $115 billion in 2027, more than doubling and growing faster than Nvidia.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e271\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e255\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Faster growth at a competitor could bear on Nvidia's future share and revenue growth.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"Micron said it did not expect tightness in the memory-chip market to ease before 2028.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e272\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\